                                "sense_id": "9b399527-8b39-3329-87eb-210efd5c7bd4",
                                "text": "The early white settlers of North America built wooden chutes, or troughs, for carrying water to power the gristmills and to transport logs down steep mountainsides. They called these artificial channels flumes."
